claimed: intent-frame-typed-values — the blocker the first caller found, and the one that makes "a filled frame can be acted on" untrue today. Slot[A] knows its type, parses an answer to prove it is acceptable, and then Frame stores the raw TEXT: a caller that wants the date parses it a second time, with the same reference day, and no type says so. Fix it without a cast -- the operator rule is explicit and this is exactly the shape that invites one. Options to weigh rather than assume: a type-indexed map keyed by the Slot itself, Frame carrying a tuple of its slots types, or a Filled[A] pairing a slot with its parsed value in a heterogeneous list. Whatever wins must keep Frame.answer refusing to store what did not parse, since that property is the one the consumer asked for by name.
